{:edb/db-before-t 401 :edb/db-after-t 402 :edb/tx-data [[13194139533714 50 #inst "2026-10-04T18:23:29.471Z" 13194139533714 true] [17592186096667 1020 #edb/ref 17592186247978 13194139533714 true] [17592186096667 1020 #edb/ref 17592186247985 13194139533714 true] [17592186096668 1020 #edb/ref 17592186247992 13194139533714 true] [17592186096668 1020 #edb/ref 17592186247996 13194139533714 true] [17592186096668 1020 #edb/ref 17592186247999 13194139533714 true] [17592186247978 1017 #edb/ref 17592186247979 13194139533714 true] [17592186247978 1089 "q-11932" 13194139533714 true] [17592186247978 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533714 true] [17592186247978 1100 "Given that $g(x)=ln⁡{x}^{2}$, find $\\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}.$" 13194139533714 true] [17592186247978 1113 #uuid "41d94fb1-0796-5126-8532-2f9de9e221a2" 13194139533714 true] [17592186247978 1138 false 13194139533714 true] [17592186247978 1145 "First, we express $g(x)$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ng=ln⁡u,\\,u={x}^{2}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}u}=\\frac{1}{u},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2x.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{u}\\cdot 2x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\cdot 2x \\\\  & =\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cancel{x}}{x\\cdot \\cancel{x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533714 true] [17592186247979 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247980 13194139533714 true] [17592186247979 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247981 13194139533714 true] [17592186247979 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247982 13194139533714 true] [17592186247979 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247983 13194139533714 true] [17592186247979 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247984 13194139533714 true] [17592186247979 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533714 true] [17592186247979 1041 "selection" 13194139533714 true] [17592186247979 1104 #edb/ref 17592186247983 13194139533714 true] [17592186247979 1110 #uuid "25d52288-4288-5c92-9b85-b241ab27bd90" 13194139533714 true] [17592186247980 1034 "\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}" 13194139533714 true] [17592186247980 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533714 true] [17592186247980 1111 #uuid "f381c761-2e10-53f1-9d4a-9e7800aec038" 13194139533714 true] [17592186247981 1034 "\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}" 13194139533714 true] [17592186247981 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533714 true] [17592186247981 1111 #uuid "c70a23de-9f2e-522c-abfc-b088d88f14a4" 13194139533714 true] [17592186247982 1034 "\\frac{1}{x}" 13194139533714 true] [17592186247982 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533714 true] [17592186247982 1111 #uuid "2d71c6ca-678c-552b-8d0a-779c3b04815f" 13194139533714 true] [17592186247983 1034 "\\frac{2}{x}" 13194139533714 true] [17592186247983 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533714 true] [17592186247983 1111 #uuid "1c525a40-4a7d-5469-b35c-f3e6eb0e5671" 13194139533714 true] [17592186247984 1034 "2xln⁡{x}^{2}" 13194139533714 true] [17592186247984 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533714 true] [17592186247984 1111 #uuid "2e1b15af-1738-5f1a-afb6-83531eb443b6" 13194139533714 true] [17592186247985 1017 #edb/ref 17592186247986 13194139533714 true] [17592186247985 1089 "q-150015" 13194139533714 true] [17592186247985 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139533714 true] [17592186247985 1100 "Find the equation of the tangent to the curve $f(x)=ln⁡(2-x)$ at the point $(1,0).$" 13194139533714 true] [17592186247985 1113 #uuid "21f3cce3-d0bf-56b4-b9d5-792bbb5193fe" 13194139533714 true] [17592186247985 1138 false 13194139533714 true] [17592186247985 1145 "First, we express $f(x)$ as the composite function\n\n$$\nf=ln⁡u,\\,u=2-x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}=\\frac{1}{u},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-1.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{u}\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2-x}\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x-2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope $m$ of the tangent line at the point where $x=1$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=1} & ={\\frac{1}{x-2}|}_{x=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(1)-2} \\\\  & =-1\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the slope of the tangent line at the point $(1,0)$ is $m=-1.$ Now, we find the equation of the tangent at that point:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-0 & =(-1)\\cdot (x-1) \\\\ y & =-x+1\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533714 true] [17592186247986 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247987 13194139533714 true] [17592186247986 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247988 13194139533714 true] [17592186247986 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247989 13194139533714 true] [17592186247986 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247990 13194139533714 true] [17592186247986 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247991 13194139533714 true] [17592186247986 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533714 true] [17592186247986 1041 "selection" 13194139533714 true] [17592186247986 1104 #edb/ref 17592186247990 13194139533714 true] [17592186247986 1110 #uuid "d3087ae0-d165-5afc-8bc6-061639664776" 13194139533714 true] [17592186247987 1034 "y=x-1" 13194139533714 true] [17592186247987 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533714 true] [17592186247987 1111 #uuid "ecf43511-e31f-5d6d-893e-006e0d204eab" 13194139533714 true] [17592186247988 1034 "y=2x" 13194139533714 true] [17592186247988 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533714 true] [17592186247988 1111 #uuid "7eb98203-e8bd-50b5-8687-f8773184c875" 13194139533714 true] [17592186247989 1034 "y=x+1" 13194139533714 true] [17592186247989 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533714 true] [17592186247989 1111 #uuid "e1424c1c-6dfb-5277-8789-3ae4c08adda1" 13194139533714 true] [17592186247990 1034 "y=-x+1" 13194139533714 true] [17592186247990 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533714 true] [17592186247990 1111 #uuid "9b6d1e0d-8be8-5230-95e1-dab4898bd164" 13194139533714 true] [17592186247991 1034 "y=-x" 13194139533714 true] [17592186247991 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533714 true] [17592186247991 1111 #uuid "5ac0a9e2-390d-5ca7-8df8-64efe5f989f1" 13194139533714 true] [17592186247992 1017 #edb/ref 17592186247993 13194139533714 true] [17592186247992 1089 "q-310149" 13194139533714 true] [17592186247992 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533714 true] [17592186247992 1100 "Given that $y=log⁡({x}^{5}-2),$ find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ in terms of $x.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533714 true] [17592186247992 1113 #uuid "064aa851-fad2-5beb-a8c7-4269d81d295b" 13194139533714 true] [17592186247992 1138 false 13194139533714 true] [17592186247992 1145 "First, we express $y$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ny=log⁡(u),\\,u={x}^{5}-2.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=\\frac{1}{uln⁡(10)},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=5{x}^{4}.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{uln⁡(10)}\\cdot 5{x}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{5{x}^{4}}{({x}^{5}-2)ln⁡(10)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533714 true] [17592186247993 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247994 13194139533714 true] [17592186247993 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247995 13194139533714 true] [17592186247993 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533714 true] [17592186247993 1041 "field-1" 13194139533714 true] [17592186247993 1104 #edb/ref 17592186247995 13194139533714 true] [17592186247993 1110 #uuid "f58a6d02-3e67-555d-9c59-624054843415" 13194139533714 true] [17592186247994 1034 "\\frac{5x^4}{x^5-2}" 13194139533714 true] [17592186247994 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533714 true] [17592186247994 1111 #uuid "39b3fc3b-89d9-58c4-ad78-9e6dfa48b59f" 13194139533714 true] [17592186247995 1034 "\\frac{5x^4}{(x^5-2)\\ln(10)}" 13194139533714 true] [17592186247995 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533714 true] [17592186247995 1111 #uuid "852ff590-2cf1-56cf-be26-4feb2441563d" 13194139533714 true] [17592186247996 1017 #edb/ref 17592186247997 13194139533714 true] [17592186247996 1089 "q-341694" 13194139533714 true] [17592186247996 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139533714 true] [17592186247996 1100 "Given that $y={log}_{4}⁡(\\sqrt{7x}),$ find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$  in terms of $x.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533714 true] [17592186247996 1113 #uuid "0ae9e168-e07a-5c2c-b242-60b8c0d52457" 13194139533714 true] [17592186247996 1138 false 13194139533714 true] [17592186247996 1145 "First, we express $y$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ny={log}_{4}⁡(u),\\,u=\\sqrt{7x}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=\\frac{1}{uln⁡(4)},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{7}{2\\sqrt{7x}}.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{uln⁡(4)}\\cdot \\frac{7}{2\\sqrt{7x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{7x}ln⁡(4)}\\cdot \\frac{7}{2\\sqrt{7x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{2\\cdot 7xln⁡(4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{7}}{2\\cdot \\cancel{7}xln⁡(4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2xln⁡(4)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533714 true] [17592186247997 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247998 13194139533714 true] [17592186247997 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533714 true] [17592186247997 1041 "field-1" 13194139533714 true] [17592186247997 1104 #edb/ref 17592186247998 13194139533714 true] [17592186247997 1110 #uuid "305b9e15-be51-5cbf-8746-5cb3a92cf499" 13194139533714 true] [17592186247998 1034 "\\frac{1}{2x\\ln(4)}" 13194139533714 true] [17592186247998 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533714 true] [17592186247998 1111 #uuid "f5ef82dd-f11b-5b24-8748-035aeac1972e" 13194139533714 true] [17592186247999 1017 #edb/ref 17592186248000 13194139533714 true] [17592186247999 1089 "q-51317" 13194139533714 true] [17592186247999 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533714 true] [17592186247999 1100 "Find ${y}^{′}$ for $y=log⁡(1-x).$" 13194139533714 true] [17592186247999 1113 #uuid "4fb12260-0edc-575d-9430-0fcd1d7f49c9" 13194139533714 true] [17592186247999 1138 false 13194139533714 true] [17592186247999 1145 "First, we express $y$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ny=log⁡u={log}_{10}⁡(u),\\,u=1-x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=\\frac{1}{uln⁡(10)},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-1.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{uln⁡(10)}\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(1-x)ln⁡(10)}\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{(1-x)ln⁡(10)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533714 true] [17592186248000 1000 #edb/ref 17592186248001 13194139533714 true] [17592186248000 1000 #edb/ref 17592186248002 13194139533714 true] [17592186248000 1000 #edb/ref 17592186248003 13194139533714 true] [17592186248000 1000 #edb/ref 17592186248004 13194139533714 true] [17592186248000 1000 #edb/ref 17592186248005 13194139533714 true] [17592186248000 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533714 true] [17592186248000 1041 "selection" 13194139533714 true] [17592186248000 1104 #edb/ref 17592186248001 13194139533714 true] [17592186248000 1110 #uuid "9d2de6e4-2c0d-5c82-bc58-bd58a9be1088" 13194139533714 true] [17592186248001 1034 "-\\frac{1}{(1-x)ln⁡(10)}" 13194139533714 true] [17592186248001 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533714 true] [17592186248001 1111 #uuid "4f8408a0-0d1e-5cf0-ab14-bc5a6eab0579" 13194139533714 true] [17592186248002 1034 "(1-x)ln⁡(10)" 13194139533714 true] [17592186248002 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533714 true] [17592186248002 1111 #uuid "1a08ad94-8b67-5380-9e71-fad071fdee02" 13194139533714 true] [17592186248003 1034 "\\frac{10}{(1-x)}" 13194139533714 true] [17592186248003 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533714 true] [17592186248